          "elType": "column",
          "settings": {"_column_size":100},
          "elements": [
            {
              "id": "tr-bio-head",
              "elType": "widget",
              "widgetType": "html",
              "settings": {
                "html": "<div class=\"tr-section-head\" style=\"display:block;margin-bottom:36px\"><span class=\"tr-label\">The story<\/span><h2>From the pulpit to the range<\/h2><\/div>"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "tr-bio-body",
              "elType": "widget",
              "widgetType": "html",
              "settings": {
                "html": "<div class=\"tr-bio-block\"><p>Rabbi Raziel Cohen served in the Israel Defense Forces, where he received advanced tactical and firearms training. After completing his service and ordination, he recognized a critical gap in the American Jewish community — a lack of practical self-defense education grounded in both skill and values.<\/p><p>He founded The Tactical Rabbi to bridge that gap. His courses combine <strong>Israeli combat methodology<\/strong> with <strong>NRA-certified instruction<\/strong> and a deep understanding of the responsibilities that come with being armed.<\/p><p>With over 30 million views across social media and coverage in outlets ranging from Fox News to The Jerusalem Post, Rabbi Cohen has become one of the most recognized voices in the intersection of faith and firearms training in America.<\/p><\/div>"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
